  "issue_title": "Suppress fallback matching after stale explicit PR references",
  "issue_body": "**Context**\n\nThis PR correctly makes explicit `#N` references authoritative when they match an open PR. The remaining edge case is when a plan item explicitly names a PR number that is not in the current open queue; falling through to title/token matching could still attach that item to a different open PR. Since this change is about reducing ambiguous reconciliation, stale explicit references should probably stop matching instead of falling back.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- [ ] If a plan item explicitly references a PR number not present in `open_prs`, `_matched_pr` returns `None`.\n- [ ] Existing valid explicit `#N`, `PR #N`, and `pull request N` matches still win immediately.\n- [ ] Add regression coverage for stale explicit references with overlapping text from another open PR.\n\n**Pointers**: `agent/planner.py` `_matched_pr`, `_explicit_pr_number`; `tests/test_planner.py` queue reconciliation tests.",
